{"name":"Halloween Party","hex":"#eb6123","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"party","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person or group of people constituting one side in a legal proceeding, such as in a legal action or a contract. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A person; an individual."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To celebrate at a party, to have fun, to enjoy oneself.","To take recreational drugs."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/party"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hallowe'en Party","blocks":[{"text":"Hallowe'en Party is a mystery novel by English writer Agatha Christie, first published in the United Kingdom by the Collins Crime Club in November 1969 and in the United States by Dodd, Mead and Company later in the same year. This book was dedicated to writer P. G. Wodehouse. It has been adapted for television, radio, and most recently for the film A Haunting in Venice (2023)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c8/Hallowe%27en_Party_First_Edition_Cover_1969.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hallowe'en_Party"},{"title":"Halloween Party (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Halloween Party\" is a song originally recorded by the Japanese supergroup Halloween Junky Orchestra in 2012. Written and produced by Hyde, it was created as part of a special Halloween project led by the rock band Vamps and features over 13 well-known musicians. It was released on October 17, 2012 by Vamps' Vamprose record label. The single reached number three on the Oricon Singles Chart and was certified Gold by the RIAJ."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a9/Halloween_Party_Cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halloween_Party_(song)"},{"title":"Costume party","blocks":[{"text":"A costume party or fancy dress party is a type of party, common in contemporary Anglo culture, in which many of the guests are dressed in costume, usually depicting a fictional or stock character, or historical figure. Such parties are popular in the United States, United Kingdom, Canada, Australia, Ireland and New Zealand, especially during Halloween."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Bee_and_Terminator_fancy_dress_costumes.jpg/330px-Bee_and_Terminator_fancy_dress_costumes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Costume_party"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c8/Hallowe%27en_Party_First_Edition_Cover_1969.jpg/250px-Hallowe%27en_Party_First_Edition_Cover_1969.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c8/Hallowe%27en_Party_First_Edition_Cover_1969.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c8/Hallowe%27en_Party_First_Edition_Cover_1969.jpg/250px-Hallowe%27en_Party_First_Edition_Cover_1969.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHallowe'en_Party_First_Edition_Cover_1969.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a9/Halloween_Party_Cover.png/250px-Halloween_Party_Cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a9/Halloween_Party_Cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a9/Halloween_Party_Cover.png/250px-Halloween_Party_Cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHalloween_Party_Cover.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.